<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK facilities management companies operate in a demanding environment - managing multiple sites, coordinating mobile engineers, and maintaining compliance across a complex portfolio of assets and contracts. The FM companies winning contracts right now are the ones using technology to prove efficiency, demonstrate compliance, and give clients real-time visibility. Yet many UK FM providers still rely on a tangle of legacy CAFM systems, paper job sheets, and spreadsheets for compliance tracking that create delays and gaps in service delivery.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf CAFM software is built for the average FM company, not your specific operation. Generic packages don't understand your unique SLA structures, your specific compliance requirements across different client sectors, or the way your engineers actually work on site. Job scheduling tools handle simple dispatch but can't optimise routes across multiple contracts or account for engineer skills and certifications. Compliance tracking is often a separate module that doesn't connect to your asset records or job history. Engineer mobile apps are clunky, require constant connectivity, and force engineers to work around the software rather than with it. The result is account managers spending evenings reconciling job data and compliance managers dreading audit season.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK facilities management companies that streamlines the entire service delivery lifecycle. From job scheduling and asset tracking to compliance management and invoice automation, we build systems that fit your exact workflows. We understand FM - from the engineer's van to the client's boardroom - and we build software that integrates with your existing accounting and job costing systems. Whether it's a bespoke engineer mobile app that works offline in plant rooms and syncs job completions automatically, or a client portal that gives facility managers real-time visibility into job status and compliance certificates, bespoke software fits your processes.</p>
<p>FM compliance carries serious consequences. LOLER inspections, PUWER examinations, fire safety checks, COSHH assessments, and asbestos registers all have statutory deadlines and specific record-keeping requirements. A lapsed LOLER inspection on a lifting asset isn't just a paperwork gap - it's a safety risk and a legal liability. Bespoke software tracks every inspection and certificate, sends automated renewal alerts, and generates audit-ready compliance reports for every asset and site. Engineers can't close a job on a non-compliant asset without recording the issue, and clients see compliance status in real time through their portal.</p>
<p>A UK hard FM provider with 80 engineers across 200 managed sites was struggling to produce accurate compliance reports for a major retail client, with three compliance near-misses on fire safety inspections in six months. We built a bespoke FM platform with an offline engineer app, automated compliance tracking, and a client portal. Compliance certificate tracking became fully automated with 28-day expiry alerts, job scheduling efficiency improved by 18% through route optimisation, and the client portal reduced account management calls by 40%. The provider won a contract extension based on the improved compliance visibility and reporting.</p>
<p>Facilities management is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear ROI. Every job, every asset, and every inspection generates data. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into efficient scheduling, automated compliance, and real-time visibility that wins and retains contracts.</p>

